    "answer_baseline": "Based on the provided context, whether religious instruction is allowed depends on the type of government funding and institution setup:\n\n* **Wholly State-Funded Institutions:** No religious instruction shall be provided in any educational institution that is wholly maintained out of State funds [Article 28(1)]. However, religious instruction is allowed if the institution is administered by the State but was established under an endowment or trust requiring religious instruction [Article 28(2)].\n* **State-Aided Institutions:** In an educational institution receiving aid out of State funds, religious instruction may be imparted, but no person attending can be required to participate in it (or attend religious worship) unless they have given consent, or if a minor, their guardian has given consent [Article 28(3)].",
